In his original post, Jethro said his character was a Valk, so IMO a wish
for the Eye of the Aethiopica wouldn't be worth it unless he had lots of
wishes, because the Valk's quest artifact, The Orb of Fate, grants level
teleport when invoked, like RS14 mentioned.  The EyeOfA would have the
advantage that he wouldn't need teleport control, and would also have the
other effects of magic resistance & mana regen, and together with the
OrbOfFate would effectively let him level teleport twice as frequently,
rather than waiting for the invocation timeout.  So if he's neutral, and
has a few wishes available, it might be worth wishing for the EyeOfA; but
if wishes are scarce, I probably wouldn't use one on the EyeOfA -
especially as wishing for artifacts can easily have no return.

And I just gotta say, it's no fair neutrals get all the good artifacts.


